      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The 20th-century labor movement significantly advanced American democracy by advocating for essential rights like collective bargaining and the right to vote for all, not just property owners. This advocacy directly led to the expansion of the middle class through the fight for better working conditions, higher wages, and crucial social safety nets like Social Security. In essence, by demanding better economic power, the movement forced political and social reforms that fundamentally democratized the American system and supported the rise of the middle class.",
